  "identity_policy": "PER_DELIVERY",
  "policy_note": "Annotations fragment bowler identity across multiple person-ids. Under PER_DELIVERY, identity is resolved inside each contiguous event=='is bowling' window, because a video contains two different bowlers (one per over). Frames annotated as bowler under a different id inside a window are counted as fragmented_frames_excluded and are NOT scored as misses, so accuracy uses a conservative denominator. action_window_frames is the evaluation set: it deliberately covers only frames inside a bowling action, which is the semantically correct unit for 'did the system pick the bowler during his delivery'. It is a subset of all bowler-role frames (scored_fraction_of_bowler_frames), which also include the bowler standing at the mark or walking back -- those frames are not evaluated.",
  "not_biomechanics_ground_truth": "This is identity/bbox ground truth only. It contains no per-delivery biomechanical labels, so no biomechanics accuracy may be derived from it.",
